m]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]test_suite_tier1.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/test_suite_tier1.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-fp[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-fp/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Static import-graph selection engine[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]engine[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]engine: build the cached import-graph selector, its depth-bounded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reverse closure, the broadening/escalation rules, and the JSON selection[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]manifest, plus the tools/select_tests CLI. No runner or Justfile [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]behavior changes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Curated contract/audit test set[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: add the `contract` pytest marker, curate the repository-wide [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]audit tests behind it to a measured serial-runtime budget, generate a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]committed manifest from the marker, and add drift and budget guards.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Scoped run mode and the no-lease path[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]runner[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine, contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]runner: add a `scoped` mode to tools/run_pytest that runs the selection [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]serially with the suite-gate explicitly disabled, escalates to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]governed full lane when the selection is too large, and never queues for[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tokens.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]just check / just check-full split[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]check-split[dim] · [dim][/dim]after runner[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]check-split: repoint `just check` at the scoped lane, add `just [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]check-full` carrying today's exhaustive behaviour, and update [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs/development.md, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, and the CI guard tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Selection health metrics and false-negative detection[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]health[dim] · [dim][/dim]after runner[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]health: persist selection manifests to a durable host-local store, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]detect when a full run fails a test a recent scoped run excluded, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add `just selection-health` to summarize coverage, escalation, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]false-negative rates.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Coverage-context ground truth for selection[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]contexts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine, health[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contexts: add --cov-context=test to the CI coverage leg, publish the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]contexts database as an artifact, and teach the engine to prefer [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]per-test coverage ground truth over the static closure when a fresh [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]baseline is available.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Two-speed verification policy in SASE memory[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]pol